0..51 Comment "//! This source defines shared string declarations."
52..55 Comment "//!"
56..133 Comment "//! Every string source reads byte storage through these declarations. A copy"
134..209 Comment "//! does not expose another string\'s write. Short strings use inline bytes."
210..256 Comment "//! Long strings share a buffer until a write."
257..322 Comment "//! Both follow the small-string representations of C++ and Rust."
323..326 Comment "//!"
327..405 Comment "//! `Repr` selects byte storage. The source provides byte functions and inline"
406..419 Comment "//! capacity."
420..423 Comment "//!"
424..502 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]"
